  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "The Bureau of Cyberspace and Digital Policy released a \"Risk Management Profile for Artificial Intelligence and Human Rights\" as a practical guide for organizations to design, develop, deploy, use, and govern AI consistent with international human rights. The bureau describes its role as leading and coordinating foreign policy on cyberspace and digital technologies, including AI, and promoting safe, responsible, secure, and rights-respecting AI. In 2025 X posts, it said the United States supports AI governance that drives innovation, creates opportunities, and avoids over-regulation. Other 2025 posts stated that transformative technologies like AI fuel innovation and that the United States is leading the AI revolution and setting the global standard.",
   "sids": [
